{"strongs": "H5971", "word": "עַם", "translit": "am", "root": "עמם", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun [masculine]", "gloss": "kinsman", "definition": "II. [ עַם ] noun [masculine] kinsman ** later development of I. עַם RS K 58; 2nd ed. 72 . (on father's side) (Arabic paternal uncle , etc., see I. עמם ; compare perhaps Tel Amarna ammu , kinsmen (?) ; on Nabataean עם ancestor compare Lzb 151, 499 ; see also especially Nes Eg 187, ZAW xvi (1896), 322f. Krenkel ib. viii (1888), 280-84 ); — suffix עַמִּי in בֶּןעַֿמִּי (q. v.), and proper name following; elsewhere plural suffix עַמֶּיךָ Num 27:13 ; Num 31:2 ( Lev 19:16 read עַמְּךָ ᵐ5 ⅏ ), + (possibly) עֲמָָמֶיךָ Judg 5:14 עַמָּיו Gen 25:8 + 15 t., עַמֶּיהָ Gen 17:14 + 3 t.; read עַמֶּי (for ᵑ0 עַמִּי , I. עַם ; compare Krenkel l.c. 281 ) Gen 49:29 and perhaps Judg 14:3 (compare Lev 21:14 ); according to Buhl Kit also 2Kgs 4:13 — father's kinsmen: וַיֵּאָסֵף אֶלעַֿמָּיו Gen 25:8 (of joining kinsmen in Sh®°ôl ), so v Gen 25:17 ; Gen 35:29 ; Gen 49:33 ; Num 20:24 ; Deut 32:50 , compare Gen 49:29 (see above), Num 27:13 ; Num 31:2 ; Deut 32:50 (all P ); וְנִכְרְתָה הַנֶּפֶשׁ מֵעַמֶּיהָ Gen 17:4 (severed from living kinsmen), so Lev 7:20 ; Lev 7:21 ; Lev 7:23 ; Lev 7:27 ; Lev 19:8 ; Lev 23:29 ; Num 9:13 , מִקֶּרֶב עַמֶּיהָ Exod 31:14 , compare Exod 30:33 ; Exod 30:38 ; Lev 17:9 (all PH); מֵעַמָּיו יִקַּח אִשָּׁה Lev 21:14 ( H ), and perhaps Judg 14:3 (simile I. עַם : [ םָ֯ , הָּ֯ ] מִקֶּרֶב עַמּוֺ Lev 17:4 ; Lev 17:10 ; Lev 18:29 +); other combinations Judg 5:14 (si vera lectio read perhaps בְּעַמֶּ֑ךָ , see I. עַם 2 d ), Lev 21:1 ; Lev 21:4 ; Lev 21:15 ( H ), Ezek 18:18 and (perhaps) 2Kgs 4:13 . — בֶּןעַֿמִּי perhaps = son of my kinsman ; on proper name with עַם see Gray Prop. N. 41 ff .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6147')\">BDB6147</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5971')\">H5971</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6146')\">BDB6146</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6148')\">BDB6148</entry></div><p> II. [<bdbheb>עַם</bdbheb>] <b>noun [masculine]</b> <highlightword>kinsman</highlightword> <div class=\"remarks\"><b>**</b>later development of I. <bdbheb>עַם</bdbheb> RS<sup>K 58; 2nd ed. 72</sup>. (on father's side) (Arabic <placeholder3925/> <highlight>paternal uncle</highlight>, etc., see  I. <bdbheb><reflink>עמם</reflink></bdbheb>; compare perhaps Tel Amarna <transliteration><highlight>ammu</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>kinsmen (?)</highlight>; on Nabataean <bdbheb>עם</bdbheb> <highlight>ancestor</highlight> compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ldzb')\">Lzb<sup>151, 499</sup></lookup>; see also especially <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Nes')\">Nes<sup>Eg 187, ZAW xvi (1896), 322f.</sup></lookup> Krenkel<sup>ib. viii (1888), 280-84</sup>); — suffix <bdbheb>עַמִּי</bdbheb> in  <bdbheb><reflink>בֶּןעַֿמִּי</reflink></bdbheb> (q. v.), and proper name following; elsewhere plural suffix <bdbheb>עַמֶּיךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 27:13\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(4,27,13)\">Num 27:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Num 31:2\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(4,31,2)\">Num 31:2</ref> (<ref ref=\"Lev 19:16\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(3,19,16)\">Lev 19:16</ref> read <bdbheb>עַמְּךָ</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sam')\"><bdbheb><reflink>⅏</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>), + (possibly) <bdbheb>עֲמָָמֶיךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 5:14\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(7,5,14)\">Judg 5:14</ref> <bdbheb>עַמָּיו</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 25:8\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(1,25,8)\">Gen 25:8</ref> + 15 t., <bdbheb>עַמֶּיהָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 17:14\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(1,17,14)\">Gen 17:14</re